</section>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bilinear (Tustin) discretization</h5>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a step <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the discrete transition</p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\Delta t)=\Big(I-\tfrac{\Delta t}{2}A_{\mathrm{ct}}\Big)^{-1}\Big(I+\tfrac{\Delta t}{2}A_{\mathrm{ct}}\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>ct</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>ct</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\Delta t)=\Big(I-\tfrac{\Delta t}{2}A_{\mathrm{ct}}\Big)^{-1}\Big(I+\tfrac{\Delta t}{2}A_{\mathrm{ct}}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the depthwise impulse response (per channel <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>) with taps</p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}k_{c}[0]&amp;=(CB)_{c}+D_{c},\\
k_{c}[\ell]&amp;=(CA(\Delta t)^{\ell}B)_{c},\quad\ell=1,\dots,L_{k}{-}1,\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}k_{c}[0]&amp;=(CB)_{c}+D_{c},\\
k_{c}[\ell]&amp;=(CA(\Delta t)^{\ell}B)_{c},\quad\ell=1,\dots,L_{k}{-}1,\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">as instantiated in Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, lines 6–8.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Schur stability via bilinear transform)<span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{ct}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>ct</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{ct}}</annotation></semantics></math> is Hurwitz (all eigenvalues in the open left half-plane), then for any <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\Delta t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) is Schur-stable: <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(A(\Delta t))&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(A(\Delta t))&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Re\lambda&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℜ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Re\lambda&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for every eigenvalue <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{ct}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>ct</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{ct}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{\Delta t}{2}\lambda\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{\Delta t}{2}\lambda\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>; hence <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I-\frac{\Delta t}{2}A_{\mathrm{ct}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>ct</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-\frac{\Delta t}{2}A_{\mathrm{ct}}</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible and
<math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\Delta t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined. If <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{ct}}v=\lambda v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>ct</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{ct}}v=\lambda v</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex1a" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\Delta t)v=\frac{1+\frac{\Delta t}{2}\lambda}{1-\frac{\Delta t}{2}\lambda}\,v\;\eqqcolon\;\lambda_{d}v." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≕</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\Delta t)v=\frac{1+\frac{\Delta t}{2}\lambda}{1-\frac{\Delta t}{2}\lambda}\,v\;\eqqcolon\;\lambda_{d}v.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\coloneqq\frac{\Delta t}{2}\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\coloneqq\frac{\Delta t}{2}\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>; then <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Re\alpha&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℜ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Re\alpha&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|1+\alpha|^{2}=1+2\Re\alpha+|\alpha|^{2}\quad\text{and}\quad|1-\alpha|^{2}=1-2\Re\alpha+|\alpha|^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℜ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℜ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|1+\alpha|^{2}=1+2\Re\alpha+|\alpha|^{2}\quad\text{and}\quad|1-\alpha|^{2}=1-2\Re\alpha+|\alpha|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">so <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|1+\alpha|&lt;|1-\alpha|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|1+\alpha|&lt;|1-\alpha|</annotation></semantics></math> and therefore <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda_{d}|&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda_{d}|&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, all eigenvalues of <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\Delta t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math> lie in the open unit disk, implying
<math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(A(\Delta t))&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(A(\Delta t))&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Exponential kernel decay)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A(\Delta t)\|\leq\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A(\Delta t)\|\leq\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> in some operator norm. Then
<math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|k[\ell]\|\leq\|C\|\,\|B\|\,\alpha^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|k[\ell]\|\leq\|C\|\,\|B\|\,\alpha^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and the tail energy satisfies
<math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\ell\geq L_{k}}\|k[\ell]\|\leq\frac{\|C\|\|B\|}{1-\alpha}\,\alpha^{L_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\ell\geq L_{k}}\|k[\ell]\|\leq\frac{\|C\|\|B\|}{1-\alpha}\,\alpha^{L_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Consequence:</em> Finite <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> yields a controlled truncation error that decays geometrically.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> MS<sup id="alg1.8" class="ltx_sup">3</sup>M — Leakage-Safe Training</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.9" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Multivariate series </span><math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{x}_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐱</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{x}_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, </span><math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐱</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.148em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.148em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">ℝ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">F</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{F}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">; window </span><math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">; output </span><math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.800em">O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">;
state </span><math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.800em">N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">; mixture size </span><math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.800em">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">; layers </span><math id="alg1.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">; kernel length </span><math id="alg1.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">; width </span><math id="alg1.l1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">;
HiPPO–LegS </span><math id="alg1.l1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{ct}}\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{N\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">ct</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.148em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.148em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">ℝ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{ct}}\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{N\times N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">; splits </span><math id="alg1.l1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{tr}},\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{va}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℐ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">tr</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℐ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">va</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{tr}},\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{va}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.14" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">;
max epochs </span><math id="alg1.l1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">E</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.15" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">; patience </span><math id="alg1.l1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.16" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">; step sizes </span><math id="alg1.l1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\gamma_{e}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">γ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\gamma_{e}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.17" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">; weight decay </span><math id="alg1.l1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.800em">λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.18" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">; clip </span><math id="alg1.l1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.19" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Best parameters </span><math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">; train scalers </span><math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\mu}_{x},\bm{\sigma}_{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝝁</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝝈</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\mu}_{x},\bm{\sigma}_{x})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, </span><math id="alg1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{y},\sigma_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">σ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{y},\sigma_{y})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Dataset and scalers (train-only fit).</span><span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Build pairs </span><math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{X}_{t},\mathbf{y}_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐗</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{X}_{t},\mathbf{y}_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> with
