              <span id="alg1.l23.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">At epoch end, define
</span><math id="alg1.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{va}}(e)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{va}}|}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{va}}}\|f_{\theta}(\widetilde{\mathbf{X}}_{t})-\widetilde{\mathbf{y}}_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">va</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℐ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">va</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℐ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">va</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.800em">2</mn><mn mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{va}}(e)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{va}}|}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{va}}}\|f_{\theta}(\widetilde{\mathbf{X}}_{t})-\widetilde{\mathbf{y}}_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l23.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">.
If </span><math id="alg1.l23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{va}}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">va</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{va}}(e)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l23.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> improves the best by </span><math id="alg1.l23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;\!{\tt tol}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.148em">&gt;</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝚝𝚘𝚕</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;\!{\tt tol}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l23.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, set
</span><math id="alg1.l23.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\star}\!\leftarrow\!\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.148em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.148em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\star}\!\leftarrow\!\theta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l23.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, reset counter; else increase counter.
When counter </span><math id="alg1.l23.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.800em">≥</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq p</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l23.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, stop. Optionally set
</span><math id="alg1.l23.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{e+1}\!\leftarrow\!\beta\,\gamma_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">γ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.148em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.148em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">γ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{e+1}\!\leftarrow\!\beta\,\gamma_{e}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l23.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> on plateaus (</span><math id="alg1.l23.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">β</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l23.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">).
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">24:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Return.</span><span id="alg1.l24.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><math id="alg1.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l24.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, </span><math id="alg1.l24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\mu}_{x},\bm{\sigma}_{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝝁</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝝈</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\mu}_{x},\bm{\sigma}_{x})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l24.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, </span><math id="alg1.l24.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{y},\sigma_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">σ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{y},\sigma_{y})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l24.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">.
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> MS<sup id="alg2.8" class="ltx_sup"><span id="alg2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">3</span></sup>M — Next-Step Inference</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.9" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Trained </span><math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">; scalers </span><math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\mu}_{x},\bm{\sigma}_{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝝁</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝝈</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\mu}_{x},\bm{\sigma}_{x})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, </span><math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{y},\sigma_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">σ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{y},\sigma_{y})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">;
new window </span><math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{\mathrm{new}}\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{L\times F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐗</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.148em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.148em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">ℝ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">F</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{\mathrm{new}}\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{L\times F}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
              <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{y}}_{\mathrm{phys}}\in\mathbb{R}^{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.800em">phys</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">ℝ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">O</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{y}}_{\mathrm{phys}}\in\mathbb{R}^{O}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Standardize </span><math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{X}}=(\mathbf{X}_{\mathrm{new}}-\bm{\mu}_{x})\oslash\bm{\sigma}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐗</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">new</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝝁</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">⊘</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝝈</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{X}}=(\mathbf{X}_{\mathrm{new}}-\bm{\mu}_{x})\oslash\bm{\sigma}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Compute </span><math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{y}}=f_{\theta^{\star}}(\widetilde{\mathbf{X}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">f</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{y}}=f_{\theta^{\star}}(\widetilde{\mathbf{X}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> as in lines 12–23 of Alg. </span><a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a><span id="alg2.l4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Inverse-standardize </span><math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{y}}_{\mathrm{phys}}=\mu_{y}+\sigma_{y}\,\hat{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.800em">phys</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">σ</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{y}}_{\mathrm{phys}}=\mu_{y}+\sigma_{y}\,\hat{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">return</span><span id="alg2.l6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{y}}_{\mathrm{phys}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.800em">phys</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{y}}_{\mathrm{phys}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">.
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS4.6" class="ltx_text">II-D</span> </span><span id="S2.SS4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Depthwise Convolution and Multi-Scale Mixture</span></h3>

<section id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Embedding</h5>

<div id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first embed standardized inputs to width <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H^{(0)}=\widetilde{\mathbf{X}}\,W_{\mathrm{in}}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d},\qquad W_{\mathrm{in}}\in\mathbb{R}^{F\times d}\quad\text{(Alg.~\ref{alg:ms3m_train_math}, line~10).}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mtext>(Alg. </mtext><mtext><a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></mtext><mtext>, line 10).</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(0)}=\widetilde{\mathbf{X}}\,W_{\mathrm{in}}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d},\qquad W_{\mathrm{in}}\in\mathbb{R}^{F\times d}\quad\text{(Alg.~\ref{alg:ms3m_train_math}, line~10).}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Mixture across <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> time scales</h5>

<div id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For layer <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\{1,\dots,L_{\ell}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\{1,\dots,L_{\ell}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and component <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\{1,\dots,M\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\{1,\dots,M\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we learn a positive step
<math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t^{(\ell,m)}=\phi(\tau^{(\ell,m)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t^{(\ell,m)}=\phi(\tau^{(\ell,m)})</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., softplus of a raw parameter), form
<math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(\ell,m)}=A(\Delta t^{(\ell,m)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(\ell,m)}=A(\Delta t^{(\ell,m)})</annotation></semantics></math>, and compute taps <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{(\ell,m)}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{(\ell,m)}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> by (<a href="#S2.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). We then <em id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sum</em> components:</p>
<table id="S2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{(\ell)}[\cdot]\;=\;\sum_{m=1}^{M}k^{(\ell,m)}[\cdot]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L_{k}},\qquad\text{(Alg.~\ref{alg:ms3m_train_math}, lines~11--12).}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>(Alg. </mtext><mtext><a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></mtext><mtext>, lines 11–12).</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{(\ell)}[\cdot]\;=\;\sum_{m=1}^{M}k^{(\ell,m)}[\cdot]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L_{k}},\qquad\text{(Alg.~\ref{alg:ms3m_train_math}, lines~11--12).}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Rationale:</em> Distinct <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t^{(\ell,m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t^{(\ell,m)}</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">values</em> induce different decay/time constants, so (<a href="#S2.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Mixture across 𝑀 time scales ‣ II-D Depthwise Convolution and Multi-Scale Mixture ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) captures both fast and slow dynamics within the same receptive field.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Depthwise causal convolution</h5>

<div id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With left zero-padding (strict causality), for channel <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\{1,\dots,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\{1,\dots,d\}</annotation></semantics></math> and time <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{1,\dots,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{1,\dots,L\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(\ell)}_{t,c}=\sum_{\tau=0}^{L_{k}-1}k^{(\ell)}_{c}[\tau]\;H^{(\ell-1)}_{t-\tau,c},\quad\text{(Alg.~\ref{alg:ms3m_train_math}, line~13).}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>(Alg. </mtext><mtext><a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></mtext><mtext>, line 13).</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(\ell)}_{t,c}=\sum_{\tau=0}^{L_{k}-1}k^{(\ell)}_{c}[\tau]\;H^{(\ell-1)}_{t-\tau,c},\quad\text{(Alg.~\ref{alg:ms3m_train_math}, line~13).}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Exponential kernel decay). ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|U^{(\ell)}_{\cdot,c}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|U^{(\ell)}_{\cdot,c}\|</annotation></semantics></math> is stable and the truncation error is bounded by a geometric tail.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS5.6" class="ltx_text">II-E</span> </span><span id="S2.SS5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Gating, Cross-Channel Mixing, and Normalization</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We modulate channels using SE gating and then apply a compact GLU mixer.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SE gate</h5>

<div id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(\ell)}\!=\!\frac{1}{L}\sum_{t=1}^{L}H^{(\ell-1)}_{t,\cdot}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(\ell)}\!=\!\frac{1}{L}\sum_{t=1}^{L}H^{(\ell-1)}_{t,\cdot}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, choose a reduction <math id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define</p>
<table id="S2.E9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="S2.EGx3" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E9.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E9.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E9.1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma\!\Big(W_{2}^{(\ell)}\,\phi\big(W_{1}^{(\ell)}\,s^{(\ell)}\big)\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma\!\Big(W_{2}^{(\ell)}\,\phi\big(W_{1}^{(\ell)}\,s^{(\ell)}\big)\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E9.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E9.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E9.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in(0,1)^{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in(0,1)^{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E9.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E9.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E9.3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times\lceil d/r\rceil},\quad W_{2}^{(\ell)}\in\mathbb{R}^{\lceil d/r\rceil\times d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times\lceil d/r\rceil},\quad W_{2}^{(\ell)}\in\mathbb{R}^{\lceil d/r\rceil\times d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9c)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Apply <math id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> channel-wise: <math id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{H}^{(\ell)}_{t,\cdot}=U^{(\ell)}_{t,\cdot}\odot g^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{H}^{(\ell)}_{t,\cdot}=U^{(\ell)}_{t,\cdot}\odot g^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Residual and layer normalization</h5>

<div id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Set</p>
<table id="S2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{(\ell)}=\mathrm{LN}\!\big(H^{(\ell-1)}+\widehat{H}^{(\ell)}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.423em;" width="1.423em"><mi>LN</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{(\ell)}=\mathrm{LN}\!\big(H^{(\ell-1)}+\widehat{H}^{(\ell)}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LN}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>LN</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LN}</annotation></semantics></math> is per-time-step layer normalization:
<math id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LN}(\mathbf{z})=\gamma\odot\frac{\mathbf{z}-\mu(\mathbf{z})}{\sigma(\mathbf{z})+\epsilon}+\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>LN</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LN}(\mathbf{z})=\gamma\odot\frac{\mathbf{z}-\mu(\mathbf{z})}{\sigma(\mathbf{z})+\epsilon}+\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, with trainable <math id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\beta)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\beta)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">GLU channel mixer</h5>

<div id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We choose a hidden width <math id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=\alpha d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=\alpha d</annotation></semantics></math> with small <math id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and define</p>
<table id="S2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{(\ell)}=W_{\downarrow}^{(\ell)}\!\Big(\phi(W_{\uparrow,a}^{(\ell)}Y^{(\ell)})\odot\sigma(W_{\uparrow,g}^{(\ell)}Y^{(\ell)})\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">↑</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">↑</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{(\ell)}=W_{\downarrow}^{(\ell)}\!\Big(\phi(W_{\uparrow,a}^{(\ell)}Y^{(\ell)})\odot\sigma(W_{\uparrow,g}^{(\ell)}Y^{(\ell)})\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\uparrow,a}^{(\ell)},W_{\uparrow,g}^{(\ell)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">↑</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">↑</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\uparrow,a}^{(\ell)},W_{\uparrow,g}^{(\ell)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times h}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\downarrow}^{(\ell)}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\downarrow}^{(\ell)}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finalize the layer with</p>
<table id="S2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{(\ell)}=\mathrm{LN}\!\big(Y^{(\ell)}+Z^{(\ell)}\big),\qquad\text{(Alg.~\ref{alg:ms3m_train_math}, lines~14--16).}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.423em;" width="1.423em"><mi>LN</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>(Alg. </mtext><mtext><a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></mtext><mtext>, lines 14–16).</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(\ell)}=\mathrm{LN}\!\big(Y^{(\ell)}+Z^{(\ell)}\big),\qquad\text{(Alg.~\ref{alg:ms3m_train_math}, lines~14--16).}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS6.6" class="ltx_text">II-F</span> </span><span id="S2.SS6.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Prediction Head and Exact Mapping</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We read out only the representation at the most recent time index:</p>
<table id="S2.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E13X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{\mathrm{head}}\,H^{(L_{\ell})}_{L,\cdot}+b_{\mathrm{head}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>head</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>head</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{\mathrm{head}}\,H^{(L_{\ell})}_{L,\cdot}+b_{\mathrm{head}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E13Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{\mathrm{head}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>head</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{\mathrm{head}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times O},\quad b_{\mathrm{head}}\in\mathbb{R}^{O},\quad\hat{\mathbf{y}}\in\mathbb{R}^{O}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>head</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>O</mi></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>O</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times O},\quad b_{\mathrm{head}}\in\mathbb{R}^{O},\quad\hat{\mathbf{y}}\in\mathbb{R}^{O},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">as in Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, line 17. The mapping</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1b" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1b.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widetilde{\mathbf{X}}\mapsto H^{(0)}\mapsto\{U^{(\ell)},\widehat{H}^{(\ell)},H^{(\ell)}\}_{\ell=1}^{L_{\ell}}\mapsto\hat{\mathbf{y}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widetilde{\mathbf{X}}\mapsto H^{(0)}\mapsto\{U^{(\ell)},\widehat{H}^{(\ell)},H^{(\ell)}\}_{\ell=1}^{L_{\ell}}\mapsto\hat{\mathbf{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p1.4" class="ltx_p">is strictly causal <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>, linear in the convolutional part, and nonlinear only in channel-mixing/gating.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS7.6" class="ltx_text">II-G</span> </span><span id="S2.SS7.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Objective, Regularization, and Optimization</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a batch <math id="S2.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, we minimize standardized MSE with weight decay (equivalently, an <math id="S2.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> penalty):</p>
<table id="S2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{tr}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}|}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\big\|f_{\theta}(\widetilde{\mathbf{X}}_{t})-\widetilde{\mathbf{y}}_{t+1}\big\|_{2}^{2}\;+\;\lambda\,\|\theta\|_{2}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>tr</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{tr}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}|}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\big\|f_{\theta}(\widetilde{\mathbf{X}}_{t})-\widetilde{\mathbf{y}}_{t+1}\big\|_{2}^{2}\;+\;\lambda\,\|\theta\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">(Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, line 19). Parameters are updated with a clipped step</p>
<table id="S2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{tr}}(\theta),\quad\tilde{g}=g\cdot\min\!\big(1,c_{\max}/\|g\|\big),\quad\theta\leftarrow\theta-\gamma_{e}\,\tilde{g}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>tr</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{tr}}(\theta),\quad\tilde{g}=g\cdot\min\!\big(1,c_{\max}/\|g\|\big),\quad\theta\leftarrow\theta-\gamma_{e}\,\tilde{g},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS7.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and early stopping on validation MSE (Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, line 22).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS8.6" class="ltx_text">II-H</span> </span><span id="S2.SS8.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Inference and De-standardization</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a new window <math id="S2.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{\mathrm{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{\mathrm{new}}</annotation></semantics></math>, standardize it using train-only scalers, compute <math id="S2.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{y}}=f_{\theta^{\star}}(\widetilde{\mathbf{X}}_{\mathrm{new}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{y}}=f_{\theta^{\star}}(\widetilde{\mathbf{X}}_{\mathrm{new}})</annotation></semantics></math> as above, and invert the target scaling</p>
<table id="S2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{y}}_{\mathrm{phys}}=\mu_{y}+\sigma_{y}\,\hat{\mathbf{y}},\qquad\text{(Alg.~\ref{alg:ms3m_infer_math}, lines~1--3).}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>phys</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>(Alg. </mtext><mtext><a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></mtext><mtext>, lines 1–3).</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{y}}_{\mathrm{phys}}=\mu_{y}+\sigma_{y}\,\hat{\mathbf{y}},\qquad\text{(Alg.~\ref{alg:ms3m_infer_math}, lines~1--3).}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS9.6" class="ltx_text">II-I</span> </span><span id="S2.SS9.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Identifiability &amp; Guarantees</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We clarify what aspects of MS<sup id="S2.SS9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S2.SS9.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">3</span></sup>M are guaranteed by construction versus encouraged in practice, and which parameters are only identifiable up to benign symmetries.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Practical identifiability</h5>

<div id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With standardized inputs/targets and a last-step head, trivial offsets are handled by <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\mathrm{head}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>head</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\mathrm{head}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Depthwise SSM parameters <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B,C)</annotation></semantics></math> and the embedding <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\mathrm{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\mathrm{in}}</annotation></semantics></math> admit classical scale/permutation symmetries (e.g., <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\!\leftarrow\!\alpha C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\!\leftarrow\!\alpha C</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\!\leftarrow\!\alpha^{-1}B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\!\leftarrow\!\alpha^{-1}B</annotation></semantics></math>; channel permutations). In MS<sup id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">3</span></sup>M these are <em id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">mitigated</em>—not eliminated—by (i) separate parameter blocks with weight decay, (ii) per-time-step LayerNorm and SE gating, which fix effective channel scales, and (iii) the fixed wiring of SE/GLU and the head. Mixture time scales <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t^{(\ell,m)}{&gt;}0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t^{(\ell,m)}{&gt;}0</annotation></semantics></math> (via a positive map) are <em id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">practically</em> identifiable up to component permutation (label-switching) and small rescalings in <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B,C)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stability and boundedness</h5>

<div id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{ct}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>ct</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{ct}}</annotation></semantics></math> is Hurwitz. By bilinear (Tustin) discretization, <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\Delta t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math> is Schur-stable for any <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t{&gt;}0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t{&gt;}0</annotation></semantics></math> (Prop. <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 1 (Schur stability via bilinear transform). ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). With finite kernel support <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, each depthwise block is Finite Impulse Response (FIR) and hence Bounded-Input Bounded-Output (BIBO)-stable; with infinite support, Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Exponential kernel decay). ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> ensures geometric tail decay.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Causality</h5>

<div id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All convolutions are one-sided with left zero-padding, so <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(\widetilde{\mathbf{X}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(\widetilde{\mathbf{X}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable and uses no future inputs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Truncation control</h5>

<div id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math> be a submultiplicative operator norm (e.g., induced 2-norm) and suppose <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A(\Delta t)\|\leq\alpha{&lt;}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A(\Delta t)\|\leq\alpha{&lt;}1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|k[\ell]\|\leq\|C\|\,\|B\|\,\alpha^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|k[\ell]\|\leq\|C\|\,\|B\|\,\alpha^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the truncation error beyond <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by <math id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\|C\|\,\|B\|}{1-\alpha}\alpha^{L_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\|C\|\,\|B\|}{1-\alpha}\alpha^{L_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Exponential kernel decay). ‣ Bilinear (Tustin) discretization ‣ II-C HiPPO–LegS Kernels and Stable Discretization ‣ II Proposed Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixture (MS3M) ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Expressivity</h5>

<div id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sums of stable exponentials (arising from the multi-scale mixture) form a rich dictionary that can approximate causal fading-memory filters on compact domains; SE/GLU provide cross-channel mixing without quadratic attention cost. See, e.g., classical Laguerre/Kautz expansions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite> for fading-memory approximation results.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Data Collection and Preprocessing</span></h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Testbed and logging:</span>
As shown in Figure <a href="#S3.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ III Data Collection and Preprocessing ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we instrument an O<span id="S3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>RAN stack with a near<span id="S3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>RT RIC, a software <em id="S3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Base Station</em> (BS)/UE using <em id="S3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">srsRAN</em> on <em id="S3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Universal Software Radio Peripheral</em> (USRP) <em id="S3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Software<span id="S3.p1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>Defined Radios</em> (SDRs), a video server (MediaMTX + FFmpeg), and a controllable interferer. Unless stated otherwise, the BS operates at 2680 MHz downlink, 25 <em id="S3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Physical Resource Blocks</em> (PRBs), <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2{\times}2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2{\times}2</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="S3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Multiple<span id="S3.p1.1.9.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>Input Multiple<span id="S3.p1.1.9.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>Output</em> (MIMO), <em id="S3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Frequency<span id="S3.p1.1.10.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>Division Duplexing</em> (FDD). The interferer is implemented in C<span id="S3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">++</span>/<em id="S3.p1.1.12" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">USRP Hardware Driver</em> (UHD) and injects random<span id="S3.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text">-</span>length <em id="S3.p1.1.14" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Orthogonal Frequency<span id="S3.p1.1.14.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>Division Multiplexing</em> (OFDM) bursts with randomized gain, sleeping <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,5]</annotation></semantics></math> ms between bursts to create intermittent co<span id="S3.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text">-</span>channel interference. Each run lasts 120 s while the UE streams video. We log (i) <em id="S3.p1.1.16" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Physical</em> (PHY)/<em id="S3.p1.1.17" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Medium Access Control</em> (MAC) KPIs from BS/UE (exported every 20 ms), (ii) FFmpeg streaming statistics, and (iii) optional packet captures. Two deployments are used: a cloudified next<span id="S3.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text">-</span>generation (xG) testbed (USRP X310; OpenStack <em id="S3.p1.1.19" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Virtual mMchines</em> (VMs)) and a lab setup (USRP B210; standalone hosts). Table <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table II ‣ III Data Collection and Preprocessing ‣ Rivaling Transformers: Multi-Scale Structured State-Space Mixtures for Agentic 6G O-RAN" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a> summarizes the dataset statistics for the considered KPIs. The dataset<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
          A version of our dataset is available at: <a href="https://ieee-dataport.org/documents/video-streaming-network-kpis-o-ran-testing" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://ieee-dataport.org/documents/video-streaming-network-kpis-o-ran-testing</a></span></span></span> is publicly available, which ensures reproducibility and facilitates further research.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.05255v1/Figures/testbed.png" id="S3.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:467/138;" width="467" height="138" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 1: </span>Virginia Tech Innovation Campus O-RAN testbed setup <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Temporal aggregation to a uniform grid:</span>
Heterogeneous logs are aligned by windowed averaging onto a common timeline. For KPI <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> with raw samples <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(t_{i},x_{i}^{(k)})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(t_{i},x_{i}^{(k)})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, a window of length <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> and stride <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> produces</p>
<table id="S3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{x}^{(k)}(t_{m})=\frac{1}{N_{m}}\!\!\sum_{i:\,t_{i}\in[t_{m},\,t_{m}+\Delta)}\!\!x_{i}^{(k)},\qquad t_{m+1}=t_{m}+\tau," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{x}^{(k)}(t_{m})=\frac{1}{N_{m}}\!\!\sum_{i:\,t_{i}\in[t_{m},\,t_{m}+\Delta)}\!\!x_{i}^{(k)},\qquad t_{m+1}=t_{m}+\tau,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">yielding uniformly spaced series <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bar{x}^{(k)}(t_{m})\}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bar{x}^{(k)}(t_{m})\}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. We left<span id="S3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>join all KPIs at <math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> to form a matrix <math id="S3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{kpi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>kpi</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{kpi}}</annotation></semantics></math> (one row per time step).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Semantics<span id="S3.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>aware missingness:</span>
Because no packet may arrive in some intervals, “UE Packet Delay” can be absent while other KPIs remain valid. We therefore <em id="S3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">retain</em> rows missing <em id="S3.p3.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">only</em> this field and impute a reserved sentinel <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math>; any row missing <em id="S3.p3.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">other</em> KPIs is <em id="S3.p3.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">dropped</em>, as it indicates a broader measurement gap.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Outlier control (IQR pruning):</span>
Per KPI, define <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{1}=\mathrm{quantile}_{0.10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>quantile</mi><mn>0.10</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{1}=\mathrm{quantile}_{0.10}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{3}=\mathrm{quantile}_{0.90}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>quantile</mi><mn>0.90</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{3}=\mathrm{quantile}_{0.90}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{IQR}=Q_{3}{-}Q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>IQR</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{IQR}=Q_{3}{-}Q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Samples outside</p>
<table id="S3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\,Q_{1}-1.5\,\mathrm{IQR},\;Q_{3}+1.5\,\mathrm{IQR}\,]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>IQR</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>IQR</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\,Q_{1}-1.5\,\mathrm{IQR},\;Q_{3}+1.5\,\mathrm{IQR}\,]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">are removed prior to forming sequences. This decile<span id="S3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>based rule dampens heavy tails without erasing typical dynamics.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sequential samples for one<span id="S3.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>step forecasting:</span>
From the cleaned table with <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> KPIs, we extract contiguous sequences of length <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{seq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>seq</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{seq}}</annotation></semantics></math> (we use <math id="S3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{seq}}{=}28" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>seq</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>28</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{seq}}{=}28</annotation></semantics></math>) only if all within<span id="S3.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>window gaps equal <math id="S3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. For each valid index <math id="S3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\big[\bar{\bm{x}}(t_{m-N_{\mathrm{seq}}+1}),\,\ldots,\,\bar{\bm{x}}(t_{m})\big]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>seq</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big[\bar{\bm{x}}(t_{m-N_{\mathrm{seq}}+1}),\,\ldots,\,\bar{\bm{x}}(t_{m})\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E19Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bar{\bm{x}}(t_{m+1})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bar{\bm{x}}(t_{m+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Types: </span> <math id="S3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{N_{\mathrm{seq}}\times K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>seq</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{N_{\mathrm{seq}}\times K}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Yielding paired datasets <math id="S3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{x}=\{X_{m}\}_{m=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{x}=\{X_{m}\}_{m=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{y}=\{y_{m}\}_{m=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{y}=\{y_{m}\}_{m=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the RSRP task, we select the appropriate component of <math id="S3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> as the target; all covariates used by forecasters are shifted by <math id="S3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+1</annotation></semantics></math> step downstream to guarantee leakage safety.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KPI selection and splits:</span>
KPI choices follow the O<span id="S3.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>RAN End<span id="S3.p8.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>to<span id="S3.p8.1.4" class="ltx_text">-</span>End Test Specification <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>. We use contiguous tail splits for train/validation/test and fit any scalers or feature selection on <em id="S3.p8.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">train only</em> to prevent information leakage.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE II: </span>Statistical overview of measured performance indicators, with units and interpretations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<table id="S3.T2.7" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
